{
  "category": "Floating Pokémon",
  "entries": [
    {
      "text": "The fate of the ships and crew that wander into Jellicent’s habitat: all sunken, all lost, all vanished.",
      "version": "black"
    },
    {
      "text": "They propel themselves by expelling absorbed seawater from their bodies. Their favorite food is life energy.",
      "version": "white"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body is mostly seawater. It’s said there’s a castle of ships Jellicent have sunk on the seafloor.",
      "version": "black-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body is mostly seawater. It’s said there’s a castle of ships Jellicent have sunk on the seafloor.",
      "version": "white-2"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body is mostly seawater. It’s said there’s a castle of ships Jellicent have sunk on the seafloor.",
      "version": "x"
    },
    {
      "text": "The fate of the ships and crew that wander into Jellicent’s habitat: all sunken, all lost, all vanished.",
      "version": "y"
    },
    {
      "text": "Its body is mostly seawater. It’s said there’s a castle of ships Jellicent have sunk on the seafloor.",
      "version": "omega-ruby"
    },
    {
      "text": "The fate of the ships and crew that wander into Jellicent’s habitat: all sunken, all lost, all vanished.",
      "version": "alpha-sapphire"
    },
    {
      "text": "Jellicent is always hanging around fancy cruise ships and tankers, hoping to drag away its prey.",
      "version": "ultra-sun"
    },
    {
      "text": "Fishermen are terrified of Jellicent. It’s rumored to drag them into the sea and steal their lives away.",
      "version": "ultra-moon"
    },
    {
      "text": "Most of this Pokémon’s body composition is identical to sea water. It makes sunken ships its lair.",
      "version": "sword"
    },
    {
      "text": "Whenever a full moon hangs in the night sky, schools of Jellicent gather near the surface of the sea, waiting for their prey to appear.",
      "version": "shield"
    }
  ],
